Re-plants vibe-ic#1446 in flow_compliance_check.py: a terminal that is IN the
verdict scope but returned NO VERDICT AT ALL stops contributing to the gating
subset, so a P0 that measured nothing over a chain that never ran publishes
green again.

This is the reversal of the fix commit 3d717059f ("fix(#1446): a P0 that
measured nothing over a chain that never ran is not a pass"), whose entire code
change was to build `_no_verdict_ids` and add it as the second disjunct of the
gating condition. Dropping that disjunct is the smallest edit that reintroduces
the defect; `_no_verdict_ids` is deliberately left defined so the patch touches
one expression and nothing else. The surrounding code has since been
restructured (#2092 folded the two projections into `_ordering_is_gating`,
#2063 made the set membership derived rather than a literal `== "INCOMPLETE"`),
so this is that same reversal expressed against the live-main shape rather than
a raw `git revert`.

Re-planted, tests/test_issue1446_incomplete_in_scope_is_not_green.py goes RED on
exactly the two cases that are about this defect —
`test_a_no_verdict_p0_over_a_broken_chain_is_not_green` and
`test_the_violation_that_gates_is_named_as_gating` — while all four controls
stay green.

